    <string name="accessibility_disclosure_title">Before enabling website tracking</string>
    <string name="accessibility_disclosure_body">Unscroll asks you to enable an accessibility service to track time on websites.

It reads only the address bar of known browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Brave, Edge, Samsung Internet, Opera, and their variants). It does not read page content, messages, passwords, or what you type. It does not control the screen or detect which other apps you use.

Nothing is sent off the device. You can turn it off at any time in Android settings.</string>
    <string name="accessibility_consent">I have read this and agree to enable the service.</string>
    <string name="accessibility_service_description">Unscroll uses this service only to read the address bar of known browsers, so it can estimate time per website. It does not recognize other apps, does not read messages, typing, or passwords, and does not control the screen. Nothing is sent off the device.</string>

